1
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:04,820
An entry order waits until the price reaches a level you choose. Right-click an instrument.

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:08,680
Entry Stop Buy buys if the price rises to your level.

3
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:12,540
Entry Limit Buy buys if the price falls to your level.

4
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,770
Pick Entry Stop Buy.

5
00:00:15,870 --> 00:00:19,630
The rate starts 10 pips above the current price.

6
00:00:19,730 --> 00:00:23,760
Change the distance in pips, here to 30. The rate moves with it.

7
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:28,470
Click Buy to place the order.

8
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:32,330
It waits in the Pending tab until the price gets there.

9
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:37,190
ES means entry stop. Proximity shows how many pips the price still has to go.

10
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:43,110
Its line is above the chart, so this arrow points to it.

11
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:46,320
For a limit, pick Entry Limit Buy instead.

12
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:50,680
Now the rate starts below the price, because a limit buys cheaper.

13
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:53,060
Close the window to leave it.

